# Fleet map

If any of the first 5 non-empty lines of the user message (leading blank lines OK) is or begins with (case-insensitive) `Ти си <role>`, where `<role>` is Product, Code, Review, Release, Coord, or installbot (lowercase file name), read `.repo-rules/cursor/roles/<role lowercase>.md`, then `.repo-rules/common/`, then `docs/STATUS.md`, before doing anything.

- `docs/STATUS.md` — current snapshot (read first; wrap up the task here)
- `docs/memory/` — durable project memory (then ROADMAP, TASKS, BRIEFS below)
- `docs/ROADMAP.md` — milestones and `Now`
- `docs/TASKS.md` — open tasks; **Code priorities** section at the top = next Code work
- `docs/BRIEFS.md` — active Code briefs (started, not merged); Code reads its brief here
- `docs/HISTORY.md` — done log; open a row only if the task matches
- `docs/TESTS.md` — tests waiting for Pier (what to test, release link, version, date added)
- Rules live in `.repo-rules/` (plain files from https://github.com/PierMobayed/repo-rules). Read `.repo-rules/cursor/roles/<role>.md` + `.repo-rules/common/`. SHA in `.repo-rules/SYNCED_FROM`. Do not git pull in `.repo-rules/`. Private repos: commit `.repo-rules/` (do not gitignore). **This repo is public:** `.repo-rules/` is gitignored — local copy only; this map must not contain private rule text.
